{"id": 1266, "stem": "<div class=\"relative w-full min-w-0 max-w-full self-stretch\" id=\"question-text\"><span><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\"><mark class=\"bg-transparent dark:text-neutral-100\" data-markjs=\"true\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">A</mark> 13-year-old boy is brought to the office for evaluation of worsening scoliosis.\u00a0 He lost the ability to walk a year ago and now uses a wheelchair.\u00a0 He also has difficulty coughing effectively and taking deep breaths due to muscle weakness.\u00a0 Genetic testing previously identified a mutation in the dystrophin gene on his X chromosome.\u00a0 Histopathologic examination of his calf muscle would most likely reveal which of the following findings?\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c</p></span></div>", "options": [{"label": "A", "text": "Abnormally high intracellular glycogen"}, {"label": "B", "text": "Diffuse hypertrophic muscle fibers"}, {"label": "C", "text": "Focal accumulation of abnormal mitochondria"}, {"label": "D", "text": "Increased connective tissue deposition"}, {"label": "E", "text": "Lipid droplets within muscle fibers"}], "correctAnswer": "D", "explanation": "<div class=\"relative w-full min-w-0 max-w-full self-stretch\" id=\"question-explanation\"><span class=\"\"><div id=\"div_T99501\" style=\"overflow-x: auto; font-size: 1rem;\"><div class=\"group/triggerable\" data-is-open=\"false\"><div class=\"group/draggable\" data-is-draggable=\"true\" data-is-dragging=\"false\"><div class=\"group/resizable relative\" data-is-maximized=\"false\" data-is-resizable=\"true\" data-is-resizing=\"false\"><div class=\"relative max-w-full\"><div aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"pointer-events-none absolute left-0 top-0 bottom-0 w-8 z-10 transition-opacity duration-200 bg-gradient-to-r from-white dark:from-nbme-primary-dark-800 warm:from-egg-sour-50 to-transparent opacity-0\"></div><div aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"pointer-events-none absolute right-0 top-0 bottom-0 w-8 z-10 transition-opacity duration-200 bg-gradient-to-l from-white dark:from-nbme-primary-dark-800 warm:from-egg-sour-50 to-transparent opacity-0\"></div><div class=\"max-w-full overflow-x-auto [&amp;_td]:min-w-[8rem] [&amp;_th]:min-w-[8rem]\"><table class=\"border bg-transparent dark:text-white border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white hover:bg-transparent warm:hover:bg-transparent dark:hover:bg-transparent cursor-default mt-2 mb-3\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><tbody style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><tr class=\"hover:bg-original-nbme-400/10 warm:hover:bg-brown-700/10 dark:hover:bg-white/15\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" colspan=\"3\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\"><strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><mark class=\"bg-transparent dark:text-neutral-50\" data-markjs=\"true\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">D</mark>uchenne &amp; Becker muscular dystrophies</strong></p></td></tr><tr class=\"hover:bg-original-nbme-400/10 warm:hover:bg-brown-700/10 dark:hover:bg-white/15\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\"><strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Diagnosis</strong></p></td><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\"><strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Duchenne</strong></p></td><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\"><strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Becker</strong></p></td></tr><tr class=\"hover:bg-original-nbme-400/10 warm:hover:bg-brown-700/10 dark:hover:bg-white/15\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\"><strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Pathophysiology</strong></p></td><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" colspan=\"2\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><ul class=\"flex flex-col justify-start items-start list-inside list-disc ml-4 mb-4\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><li class=\"mb-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Mutation of dystrophin gene on X chromosome</li><li class=\"mb-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Disrupted dystrophin in muscle cytoskeleton \u2192 muscle atrophy &amp; replacement with connective tissue/fat</li></ul></td></tr><tr class=\"hover:bg-original-nbme-400/10 warm:hover:bg-brown-700/10 dark:hover:bg-white/15\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\"><strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Dystrophin function</strong></p></td><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\">Absent</p></td><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\">Reduced</p></td></tr><tr class=\"hover:bg-original-nbme-400/10 warm:hover:bg-brown-700/10 dark:hover:bg-white/15\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\"><strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Age of onset</strong></p></td><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\">Age 2-3</p></td><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\">Age 5-15</p></td></tr><tr class=\"hover:bg-original-nbme-400/10 warm:hover:bg-brown-700/10 dark:hover:bg-white/15\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\"><strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Clinical course</strong></p></td><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><ul class=\"flex flex-col justify-start items-start list-inside list-disc ml-4 mb-4\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><li class=\"mb-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Severe proximal muscle weakness (eg, Gowers sign)</li></ul><ul class=\"flex flex-col justify-start items-start list-inside list-disc ml-4 mb-4\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><li class=\"mb-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Wheelchair use by adolescence</li><li class=\"mb-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Shortened lifespan (age 20-30) from respiratory/heart failure</li></ul></td><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><ul class=\"flex flex-col justify-start items-start list-inside list-disc ml-4 mb-4\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><li class=\"mb-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Milder proximal muscle weakness</li><li class=\"mb-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Shortened lifespan (age 40-50) from heart failure</li></ul></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div></div></div></div></div><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\">This patient's severe, progressive muscle weakness and dystrophin gene mutation are consistent with <strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Duchenne muscular dystrophy</strong> (DMD), an <strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">X-linked recessive</strong> disorder that primarily affects boys.\u00a0 DMD typically results from <a class=\"hint\" data-exhibit-id=\"exhibit-hf8hsg28om7k6xc4c2a1jc6t\" href=\"#exhibit-exhibit-hf8hsg28om7k6xc4c2a1jc6t\">out-of-frame deletions</a> or other mutations that prevent production of functional dystrophin.\u00a0 In contrast, Becker muscular dystrophy usually results from in-frame deletions that allow production of a partially functional protein, causing a milder phenotype.</p><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\"><strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Dystrophin</strong> links the intracellular actin cytoskeleton to a membrane protein complex that connects to the extracellular matrix, stabilizing the muscle cell membrane during contraction.\u00a0 Its absence causes membrane injury and repeated <strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">muscle fiber necrosis</strong>, followed by regeneration and eventual replacement by <strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">fat and connective tissue</strong>.</p><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\">Symptoms usually begin at age 2\u20133\u00a0years, with delayed motor milestones, difficulty keeping up with peers, and a waddling gait due to <strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">proximal muscle weakness</strong>.\u00a0 Patients use their hands to push against their legs when rising from the floor (<strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Gowers sign</strong>).\u00a0 The calves may appear enlarged despite weakness because muscle fibers are replaced by fat and connective tissue (<strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">calf pseudohypertrophy</strong>).</p><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\">Progressive weakness often necessitates wheelchair use by adolescence.\u00a0 Weakness of the paraspinal muscles and altered posture contribute to progressive <strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">scoliosis</strong>, which, along with <strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">respiratory muscle weakness</strong>, contributes to difficulty taking deep breaths and coughing effectively.</p><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\"><strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">(Choice A)</strong>\u00a0 Abnormally high intracellular glycogen occurs in muscle glycogen storage disorders such as McArdle disease, which results from muscle glycogen phosphorylase deficiency.\u00a0 Patients typically have exercise-induced muscle pain, cramps, and sometimes myoglobinuria.</p><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\"><strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">(Choice B)</strong>\u00a0 Some surviving muscle fibers may hypertrophy in DMD.\u00a0 However, the biopsy shows variable fiber size and progressive fibrofatty replacement rather than diffuse muscle fiber hypertrophy.</p><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\"><strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">(Choice C)</strong>\u00a0 Subsarcolemmal accumulation of abnormal mitochondria produces <strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">ragged red fibers</strong> on modified Gomori trichrome staining.\u00a0 These fibers are characteristic of mitochondrial myopathies, which involve impaired oxidative phosphorylation.</p><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\"><strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">(Choice E)</strong>\u00a0 Lipid droplets within muscle fibers are characteristic of lipid storage myopathies.\u00a0 In DMD, fat accumulates primarily as adipose tissue replacing damaged muscle fibers rather than as intracellular lipid droplets.</p><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\"><strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Educational objective:</strong>Duchenne muscular dystrophy is an X-linked recessive disorder in which absent functional dystrophin causes progressive muscle fiber necrosis and weakness.\u00a0 Biopsy shows necrotic and regenerating muscle fibers along with increased connective tissue deposition.\u00a0 Replacement of muscle by fat and connective tissue causes calf pseudohypertrophy.\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c</p></span></div>", "educationalObjective": "Duchenne muscular dystrophy is an X-linked recessive disorder in which absent functional dystrophin causes progressive muscle fiber necrosis and weakness.  Biopsy shows necrotic and regenerating muscle fibers along with increased connective tissue deposition.  Replacement of muscle by fat and connective tissue causes calf pseudohypertrophy.\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c", "subject": "Pathology", "system": "Nervous System", "topic": "Duchenne dystrophy", "category": "Disorders of peripheral nerves and muscles", "peerCorrect": 21.0}